WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.071 --> 00:00:00.976
- He's smoking.

00:00:00.976 --> 00:00:01.974
They're smoking already.

00:00:01.974 --> 00:00:03.252
There's a cat smoking!

00:00:03.252 --> 00:00:05.112
- Everyone is smoking.

00:00:05.112 --> 00:00:08.027
(playful Russian music)

00:00:08.027 --> 00:00:09.279
- I don't speak Russian so I don't know

00:00:09.279 --> 00:00:10.463
how much I'm gonna be able to understand.

00:00:10.463 --> 00:00:12.274
- I think we're gonna be scolded a lot.

00:00:12.274 --> 00:00:14.650
- I'm hoping there'll
be a lot of dark humor.

00:00:17.236 --> 00:00:18.270
- Looks like it took a lot more effort

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.243
than some of the cartoons
I watched growing up.

00:00:20.243 --> 00:00:21.915
- I don't know whether it's day or night.

00:00:21.915 --> 00:00:24.632
- I feel like it's about
this guy being sad and lonely

00:00:24.632 --> 00:00:25.677
looking for friends.

00:00:25.677 --> 00:00:27.464
- His face looks so sad and miserable.

00:00:27.464 --> 00:00:29.159
- There's a darkness there.

00:00:29.159 --> 00:00:30.065
- [Both] Woah!

00:00:30.065 --> 00:00:31.876
- What is that dinosaur!?

00:00:31.876 --> 00:00:32.934
- Is he sad?

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:33.776
Or is he happy?

00:00:33.776 --> 00:00:36.051
- It's like he's getting served
divorce papers or something.

00:00:36.051 --> 00:00:37.584
- Oh my god look at that little guy.

00:00:37.584 --> 00:00:39.163
- He would be cute in the daytime

00:00:39.163 --> 00:00:41.149
and really freaky at night.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:45.640
- Everyone is smoking!

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:46.539
- Why is everyone smoking

00:00:46.539 --> 00:00:48.292
and why are the cigarettes backwards?

00:00:48.292 --> 00:00:49.558
Is that how Russian people smoke?

00:00:49.558 --> 00:00:50.628
- [Guy] Oh my god.
- That's like super hardcore.

00:00:50.628 --> 00:00:52.122
- I don't trust that wolf.

00:00:52.122 --> 00:00:53.887
- I feel like the wolf is the bad guy.

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:54.913
- So this is the healthy guy.

00:00:54.913 --> 00:00:55.915
He's not smoking.

00:00:55.915 --> 00:00:56.886
He's riding a bike.

00:00:56.886 --> 00:00:58.326
- I think he's gonna eat the bunny.

00:00:58.326 --> 00:01:00.519
- This seems like very Looney Tunesesque

00:01:00.519 --> 00:01:01.460
to me.
- [Girl] Yes.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:04.595
- I think it probably
is more inappropriate

00:01:04.595 --> 00:01:06.336
for today's audience.

00:01:09.419 --> 00:01:10.296
- He's so cute!

00:01:10.296 --> 00:01:12.385
- He doesn't have legs but he has feet.

00:01:12.385 --> 00:01:13.527
- Looks like this.

00:01:13.527 --> 00:01:14.780
- Yeah, like a little chipmunk.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:17.796
- It's kinda like a weird acid trip?

00:01:17.796 --> 00:01:19.792
- It's like a children's
book but animated.

00:01:19.792 --> 00:01:21.393
- I can't think of an American cartoon

00:01:21.393 --> 00:01:22.721
that really looks like this.

00:01:22.721 --> 00:01:24.114
- This is the most graceful fall.

00:01:24.114 --> 00:01:27.280
- I bet Russian people loved it in 1965.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:29.107
- I love it in 2016.

00:01:29.107 --> 00:01:31.061
- He kind of reminded
me of Winnie the Pooh.

00:01:31.061 --> 00:01:32.344
- Is it Winnie the Pooh?

00:01:32.344 --> 00:01:33.308
- [Voiceover] It is, yeah.
Oh my god.

00:01:33.308 --> 00:01:35.272
- Ohh.
- [Girl] Yeah.

00:01:38.311 --> 00:01:39.532
- I'm just impressed with like

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:40.837
the quality of this.

00:01:40.837 --> 00:01:42.107
- This looks like a video game.

00:01:42.107 --> 00:01:44.429
- I'm worried about those animals' safety.

00:01:44.429 --> 00:01:46.457
- This girl has a very
short attention span,

00:01:46.457 --> 00:01:47.850
but also she's a child.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.027
- She seems like a terror.

00:01:49.027 --> 00:01:50.001
- Someone needs to teach her

00:01:50.001 --> 00:01:51.766
how to properly play with animals.

00:01:51.766 --> 00:01:53.136
- He's going into the forest.

00:01:53.136 --> 00:01:54.986
- Oh, the bear has his own home.

00:01:54.986 --> 00:01:56.366
- He's an artisanal bear.

00:01:56.366 --> 00:01:57.875
- This bear's classier than me.

00:01:57.875 --> 00:01:58.606
- Yeah, that's true.

00:01:58.606 --> 00:01:59.721
- [Girl] Look at him drinking tea.

00:01:59.721 --> 00:02:01.764
- She hasn't learned yet how to treat

00:02:01.764 --> 00:02:03.041
other living beings.

00:02:03.041 --> 00:02:04.783
- She's gonna come across
that bear and I think

00:02:04.783 --> 00:02:06.362
he's gonna teach her some life lessons.

00:02:06.362 --> 00:02:08.498
- I honestly wish our
cartoons were like this.

00:02:08.498 --> 00:02:09.496
This is so cool.

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:10.584
- I'm like really impressed with just

00:02:10.584 --> 00:02:12.966
how the cartoons look,
like the animations.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:14.436
- I might binge watch it.

00:02:14.436 --> 00:02:15.438
- You would binge watch this?

00:02:15.438 --> 00:02:16.322
- [Guy] I would binge watch this.

00:02:16.322 --> 00:02:19.536
- I think they're like way
cooler than American cartoons.

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:24.517
(air swishing and metal squeaking)

